# raw dumps and derived data — huge, never commit.
# The globs must cover every geographic box, not just the first one: these
# started as data/flights and data/decomposition, and when the ECAC box added
# data/flights_ecac and data/decomposition_ecac they fell straight through the
# ignore rules. 15 GB of parquet and, far worse, PER-FLIGHT rows sat one
# `git add -A` away from being committed.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/flights*/
# ERA5 wind cache (Mac lab only)
data/era5*/
# per-flight decomposition output (derived, regenerable, and per-flight rows
# must never leave the lab — the published product is always aggregate)
data/decomposition*/
data/contrail*/
# Rete di sicurezza PER TIPO DI FILE, non per nome di cartella: la regola per
# nome ha gia' fallito otto volte, l'ultima con data/contrail_phasea/ che nessun
# pattern copriva. I dati per singolo volo sono sempre parquet o netCDF; i file
# di riferimento tracciati sono solo csv e json.
data/**/*.parquet
data/**/*.nc
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
refs/
# Unsent draft correspondence. Publishing the advance-notice letters AFTER they
# are sent is good for transparency; publishing the drafts before is not.
# Remove this line deliberately, per file, once a letter has actually gone out.
outreach/
# Internal working notes: Italian, home hardware details, incident RCAs.
# The public artefact is the methodology page, not the lab notebook.
reports/
.DS_Store
# Operational runbook: launch sequence, DNS steps, and the status of
# correspondence not yet sent. Internal, same reasoning as outreach/.
DEPLOY.md

# Per-airport data bundles: derived data, regenerable, and large.
exports/
